 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/488-blackwood","name":"Blackwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T07:57:07-07:00","id":1234954,"title":"","content":"p.118 Both the Ranged and Thrown Attack' Disarm stunt refer to knocking the weapon into the <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">'near'</span> range increment, which does not exist (Close or Short maybe).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/972-fairlyhyperman","name":"Fairlyhyperman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T09:22:16-07:00","id":1234981,"title":"","content":"p. 174: miss type of Lugh L\u00e1mhfhada as <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Health</span> Lugh L\u00e1mhfhada .<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24326-jester","name":"Jester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T10:55:47-07:00","id":1235012,"title":"","content":"Theirs several references to page XX In Scion Hero thats forgivabble but in Origin I think all those need to be replaced with the correct page number.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T11:11:57-07:00","id":1235020,"title":"","content":"Pg 62, first paragraph under Approaches is still referencing Arena ratings, rather than the Attribute dot allocation detailed in character creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13075-malicwanderer","name":"MalicWanderer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T12:45:21-07:00","id":1235054,"title":"","content":"On Page 98 it says<br /> <br /> Choose a single Heroic Knack appropriate to their<br /> Calling from the lists starting on p. XX<br /> <br /> Should say &quot;Mortal Knack&quot; I think","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T14:07:30-07:00","id":1235079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1233836-scion-origin-errata-thread?p=1235012#post1235012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theirs several references to page XX In Scion Hero thats forgivabble but in Origin I think all those need to be replaced with the correct page number.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I noted a couple pages back, that's deliberate. They're going to change the numbers once all this errata is in place and they know the editingwon't change the page numbers","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T03:01:19-07:00","id":1235223,"title":"","content":"Page 148, &quot;Incorporeality&quot; at the top of the page (below Occult) is indented and in the wrong font. &quot;Vulnerability&quot; has the same issue toward the bottom of the page (above Flairs).<br /> Page 152, there's a write-up for the LIKE A SIEVE flair-- an anomalous &quot;Cooldown: End of scene&quot; line,-- and then the write-up for RED HERRING begins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T04:58:48-07:00","id":1235246,"title":"","content":"I've read through earlier posts in an attempt not to overlap, but I may miss something. Sorry.<br /> <br /> Boon (p. 16): Might be better to mention that, if you are doing character creation from *this* book, you don't get any of these at all.<br /> <br /> Not the world, but The World (p. 22): The all-caps heading font makes this heading gibberish, because there is no typographical distinction between the two worlds.<br /> <br /> Knacks (p. 105 onwards): The reference to Path dots could do with a box out explanation; I presume that they appear in Hero, and that pre-vis default to one, but that is not explicitly stated. It would also be nice to include an explicit note that Hero+ can have multiple Knacks active at once, so that the references in some Knacks to conditions that can only be created by other Knacks are not redundant.<br /> <br /> A Sentinel (p. 106): Has a reference to your &quot;charge&quot;, but the Knack defining a charge does not seem to be present. (Compare &quot;quarry&quot; for Hunter, where the defining Knack is also present.)<br /> <br /> Healer (p. 107): Damage Conversion appears to be strictly better than Combat Medic, in that Damage Conversion heals all Bruised Injuries, while Combat Medic only heals one. I suspect that Combat Medic may be supposed to be a reflexive action, but it doesn't say that. It may also be that you cannot do First Aid during Combat without Combat Medic, but the current phrasing of the Knack does not suggest that. If that is the meaning, something like &quot;You may tend to an ally's wounds in the heat of battle. When you do...&quot; would be easier to follow, and it should specify what kind of action it is. (Simple, in this case, I assume.)<br /> <br /> Character Creation p. 98: The Health section says every character starts with 4 levels of Injury, but the immediately following box says that Little Mao starts with three.<br /> <br /> Modifiers to Attack/Defense Actions (p. 118): Refers to &quot;clash&quot; range, which looks like an old name for &quot;close&quot; range.<br /> <br /> Resolving Damage, p. 120-1: Characters with a Stamina Rating of 1 get an Injury box, but every character starts with a dot in Stamina, and no chance to drop it. This looks like a relic, that also affected the example.<br /> <br /> The text says that Aggravated Damage is Persistent, and the Lethal Damage is Persistent against mortal characters. However, the definition of Persistent Condition, on page 67, says that they can only be resolved with divine intervention. That makes sense for Aggravated Damage, but means that Origin-level characters can never heal Lethal Damage, and so Taken Out means Dead, because they cannot heal the condition without divine intervention. I strongly suspect that this is not the intention, because it means that mortal level characters can basically only be in one fight with lethal weapons *ever*. (If the Persistent tag is not supposed to override the given Resolution conditions, then it is meaningless for Aggravated Damage as well.)<br /> <br /> The Damage conditions all say &quot;Effect: None, beyond filling the damage level&quot;, but the examples given immediately afterwards all have specific effects. I'm really not clear what this is supposed to mean. Does each condition have an effect based on the description? Or do you choose between the Momentum and the Effect?<br /> <br /> Damage and Scale (p. 122): The explanation is repeated both before and after the heading. The explanation before the header is internally consistent, the one after is not (3 is not no greater than 2 above 0). However, the Scale table on page 66 defines skyscrapers as Scale 5, not 4 as in the earlier example. An armored car is not an example, but a main battle tank is scale 3; should an armored car be a whole scale point lower? (Possible, but the choice to make it a 3 in the second example seems reasonable.)<br /> <br /> Weapon Tags (p. 121 ff): I've spotted a lot of things here that look like relics of earlier versions of the combat system. It might be a good idea to go through all of these again, in case I missed some.<br /> <br /> Automatic (p. 122): Talks about the Empty the Clip Stunt, and contradicts the description of that stunt on page 118. The description of the stunt makes the sensible assumption that it, well, empties the clip; this description says it does not. I suspect that this description should just refer to burst fire. Also, if you roll with Complications, and choose to succeed, with a single success, what do all the ignored Complications do? Or should it add to the Difficulty?<br /> <br /> Bashing: (p. 122): Refers to the Broken and Battered Injury Conditions, which no longer seem to exist. Maybe Bruised?<br /> <br /> Lethal (p. 122): Says it cannot inflict the Bruised or Battered Conditions, but Battered seems to have gone. Says it can inflict the Scratched, Cut, or Bleeding Out Conditions, which also seem to have vanished.<br /> <br /> Sample Weapons (p. 124): Submachine guns do not have a damage type.<br /> <br /> Pushing (p. 124): Reference to Stress, which seems to have gone.<br /> <br /> Stun (p. 124): Refers to obsolete Injury Conditions.<br /> <br /> Hard (p. 125): This says two Injury Conditions. The box out on page 146 says two Bruised Injury Conditions, and Combat Medic and Doctor's Kit (p. 107) imply the same. However, the rules for Lethal damage would render Hard armour completely ineffective against Lethal weapons; they cannot inflict Bruised Conditions, so the character cannot choose to have the armour absorb the damage.<br /> <br /> The Branching Journey (p. 138): There is space missing in &quot;Lleuhis&quot; in the example paragraph at the end of the section.<br /> <br /> Defense (p. 144): Refers to Dodge, but this has no particular name on page 116.<br /> <br /> Monsters (p. 145): Refers to the Segments and Size rules, but these do not appear in this book. If they are only going to appear in Hero, the reference might be better deleted. If Size is supposed to be Scale, then it should be renamed.<br /> <br /> Hypnotic Charm (p. 152): This refers to reducing the Scale of a request, but the Intrigue rules don't mention Scale for requests at all, just Enhancements to the result. Thus, it is completely unclear what a Scale 2 request would look like. Murder every child at your an elementary school, including your own? Leave your nets and come follow me?<br /> <br /> How Should I Assign Scale (p. 153): The text is indented at the right.<br /> <br /> Tension (p. 153): This should probably be right at the beginning of the chapter, before all the references to spending it. Immediately before the Archetypes section, when the introduction has explained what the various terms mean, would be good.<br /> <br /> Men in Black (p. 154): &quot;invades the cultural consciousness&quot;, not &quot;conscience&quot;.<br /> <br /> Ahuizotl (p. 160)/Ahuzotl (p. 161): One of these is presumably a typo, but I have no idea which.<br /> <br /> Kitsune (p. 164): Do Mortal-tier Kitsune have a tail? Do they have to take Mortal Mask as their sole Knack if they want to be humans rather than foxes? Mortal Mask strongly suggests that kitsune can become human-with-a-tail without a special Knack, but Fox's Tail suggests that, until they get Legend 1, they do not have tails in human form at all. I think it would be better for base kitsune to be able to turn human-with-tail, so that the Knack is then human-without-tail, and they start with the Fox's Tail condition, rather than getting it at Legend 1.<br /> <br /> Blind Luck (p. 165): This refers to Hooves as a Complication, when it is a Condition. There are a number of other places where I suspect the same confusion, but it is less clear. A general search on Complication to check that it really was what you meant might be a good idea.<br /> <br /> Morrigan (p. 174): It is odd that a deity specifically described as a deity of war does not have the Warrior Calling, but not necessarily an error.<br /> <br /> Shiva (p. 175): Has Epic Strength listed twice, once in the correct alphabetical place, and once earlier.<br /> <br /> Karttikeya (p. 175): Epic Strength is out of order.<br /> <br /> Sarasvati (p. 175): Epic Strength is out of order.<br /> <br /> Varuna (p. 175): Epic Strength is out of order. Actually, just check all the Epic Strengths. Did the name change and get F&amp;Red? The Attribute Strength is called Might now, so it's possible that these are all misnamed, but maybe not; the Purview need not necessarily match the Attribute.<br /> <br /> Purview lists finishing with &quot;Stars, War&quot; are fun, but correct. I didn't spot any with the obvious typo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10351,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10351-dchart","user":"dchart","date":".  Edited to add more things I found, and keep everything together. 07-15-2018, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10351-dchart","name":"dchart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T07:59:34-07:00","id":1235268,"title":"","content":"On page 150, the illusion flair lists the resist roll as awareness+cunning. I'm guessing this is meant to be integrity+cunning or a dramatically appropriate ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24418-dracheau","name":"Dracheau","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T14:08:57-07:00","id":1235334,"title":"","content":"In the pantheons appendix each entry has the name of the god followed by a title (Ex: Hades, God of the Underworld) <br /> except<br /> Page 171, Ioskeha and Tawiscara.<br /> If i had to guess it would be Ioskeha, Good Mind and Tawiscara, Bad Mind. But they might have another title i dont know about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T15:58:17-07:00","id":1235359,"title":"","content":"A new set of errata.<br /> <br /> Sample Characters (p. 84 ff): The sample characters have little filled in squares next to some Skills. What does that mean? If it's a Hero rule, they shouldn't have them on these sheets.<br /> <br /> Deeds (p. 94): Why are the Deed descriptions tied to a random list of virtues that bear no relation to anything in the rules?<br /> <br /> Asset Skills, (p. 95 ff.): These are still mentioned, but seem to have disappeared from the rules. In some, but not all, of the Paths, they have been renamed to just &quot;Skills&quot;. All of the Pantheons on the list on page 95 are listed with Asset Skills, as are about half of the Origin Paths, apparently randomly. The Role Paths all appear to just say Skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10351,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10351-dchart","user":"dchart","date":". 07-15-2018, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10351-dchart","name":"dchart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T18:17:26-07:00","id":1235379,"title":"","content":"&quot;Street Rat&quot; in Origin Paths is considered derogatory; pick something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T21:14:36-07:00","id":1235416,"title":"","content":"Enigma is mentioned in various paths' Asset Skills lists, but not in the full list of skills in chapter 2. <br /> Guessing this needs removal. Same with the mention of Paths getting ranks beyond character creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11755-aquatica1000","name":"Aquatica1000","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T21:16:46-07:00","id":1235417,"title":"","content":"page 150 refers to rolling Awareness + Cunning. Awareness is not a skill or rating anywhere else in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T21:18:08-07:00","id":1235418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquatica1000</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1233836-scion-origin-errata-thread?p=1235416#post1235416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Enigma is mentioned in various paths' Asset Skills lists, but not in the full list of skills in chapter 2.<br /> Guessing this needs removal. Same with the mention of Paths getting ranks beyond character creation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Specifically under Sneak and Technology Expert on page 104.<br /> <br /> Can someone give the page reference for Paths getting ratings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T00:02:00-07:00","id":1235467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1233836-scion-origin-errata-thread?p=1235418#post1235418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone give the page reference for Paths getting ratings?</div> </div> </div> </div>For Origin Paths, on page 100, last sentence of the first paragraph under the heading. For Role Paths, page 103, last sentence of the first paragraph under the heading. Is this not something that comes up in Hero?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10351-dchart","name":"dchart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T01:21:28-07:00","id":1235478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dchart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1233836-scion-origin-errata-thread?p=1235467#post1235467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Origin Paths, on page 100, last sentence of the first paragraph under the heading. For Role Paths, page 103, last sentence of the first paragraph under the heading. Is this not something that comes up in Hero?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not that I can find in the draft document. Callings have ratings, but not Paths.<br /> <br /> So one of three changes is needed in Origins:<br /> <br /> - Drop the references to Path ratings on page 100 and 103<br /> <br /> - Include a statement of &quot;Paths are all rated at 1 at Origin level, so don't concern yourself with its rating now&quot;<br /> <br /> - Add in the seemingly missing rules for what Path ratings mechanically do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T09:55:28-07:00","id":1235976,"title":"","content":"So, I found a bunch of references to nonexistant Conditions:<br /> <br /> p. 67 mentions the &quot;Hangover&quot; condition.<br /> <br /> p. 77 mentions &quot;Addiction&quot; and &quot;Debt&quot; conditions.<br /> <br /> p. 122 mentions &quot;Aggravated Injury Conditions,&quot; but the section on damage resolution above suggests that the only difference between Aggravated and non-Aggravated ICs is that the latter are persistant.<br /> <br /> p. 125 mentions the &quot;Fatigued&quot; condition.<br /> <br /> p. 147: &quot;A Cage of Words&quot; mentions the &quot;Befuddled&quot; condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T16:47:09-07:00","id":1236204,"title":"","content":"Pg. 58 rolling dice sidebar<br /> <br /> &quot;2. The Storyguide and player agree on which Attribute is most relevant to the way the character is approaching the roll. The Storyguide might determine the Approach while the player decides the Approach, or both can simply settle on one Attribute.&quot;<br /> <br /> Say what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/488-blackwood","name":"Blackwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T20:24:16-07:00","id":1236277,"title":"","content":"Page 96: You can choose one of the <span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>example Conditions </b></span>or use them as a template to form your own. [There are no example path conditions to work from. It seems they were reduced to being a single set of general options (Path Suspended or Revoked)]<br /> <br /> Page 98: Choose one Calling from the list below or Supernatural Origin Path. [Supernatural Paths have no Callings.]<br /> <br /> Page 120: There are four general categories, corresponding to increasing levels of Complication severity: Bruised (\u22121), Injured (\u22122), and Maimed (\u22124). Beyond that, you\u2019re Taken Out. [It's unclear what we're subtracting. Is that to be removed from the dice pool? The effects suggest we're supposed to be raising the difficulty, not subtracting anything? Some effects do reduce defense, but it is unclear here.]<br /> <br /> Page 162: The modified supernatural paths give you skills and connections, but the base ones do not.<br /> <br /> Character Sheet: There's a reference to Movement Dice. Where in the book is this calculated? Page 72 references number of feet a human can move (Athletics + Highest Physical).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24416-novanailo","name":"NovaNailo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T22:37:19-07:00","id":1236307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DSPaul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1233836-scion-origin-errata-thread?p=1235976#post1235976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I found a bunch of references to nonexistant Conditions:<br /> <br /> p. 67 mentions the &quot;Hangover&quot; condition.<br /> <br /> p. 77 mentions &quot;Addiction&quot; and &quot;Debt&quot; conditions.<br /> <br /> p. 122 mentions &quot;Aggravated Injury Conditions,&quot; but the section on damage resolution above suggests that the only difference between Aggravated and non-Aggravated ICs is that the latter are persistant.<br /> <br /> p. 125 mentions the &quot;Fatigued&quot; condition.<br /> <br /> p. 147: &quot;A Cage of Words&quot; mentions the &quot;Befuddled&quot; condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I would also like clarification on this... or a list of conditions as a sidebar or something? maybe a page in the appendix?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/488-blackwood","name":"Blackwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T06:55:58-07:00","id":1236393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1233836-scion-origin-errata-thread?p=1236307#post1236307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I would also like clarification on this... or a list of conditions as a sidebar or something? maybe a page in the appendix?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi, please take commentary and questions to a different thread. This is an errata thread and for errata only. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T13:43:08-07:00","id":1236543,"title":"","content":"The versatile tag on page 124 isn't very clear in how precisely it works in the combat system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23666-turtle314","name":"Turtle314","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T21:27:10-07:00","id":1236669,"title":"","content":"Page 115, Attack Resolution, #3 says &quot;Spend successes to overcome the target's Defence, the attack is successful.&quot; The wording isn't very clear as it stands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T22:05:26-07:00","id":1236677,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this has been noted already or not. The sidebar on Virtues and Momentum on page 70 isn\u2019t clear that dice are added on top of the 1 from Momentum. <br /> <br /> Currently it could be read as a virtue is required to add any dice with Momentum. <br /> <br /> Maybe specify in the example that Sigrun gets 1 die for the Momentum and X dice for the alignment to a virtue. (I\u2019m assuming 1 die for a total of 2.) rather than just listing unnumbered bonus dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T04:50:43-07:00","id":1237083,"title":"","content":"p. 123: The &quot;Long Range&quot; tag is not limited to &quot;Ranged&quot; tag weapons.<br /> p. 122: The &quot;Arcing&quot; tag is not limited to &quot;Ranged&quot; tag weapons.<br /> <br /> (It may be better to arrange the tags by (0) cost tag &gt; all tags that depend on it; e.g: Ranged &gt; Long Range)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24416-novanailo","name":"NovaNailo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T13:27:53-07:00","id":1237241,"title":"","content":"p.36 \u201cA certain cave, human-made tunnel, or underground river<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">s</span> leads to one specific Afterlife or another.\u201d<br /> p.37 \u201cThey connect diverse locals in The World and Otherworlds.\u201d Locales<br /> p.40 \u201cIn The World, the Athenian Acropolis is as much a place of worship as tourism.\u201d I think \u201cas of tourism\u201d reads better<br /> p.44 \u201cand they know what kinds of choices will lead them to lives worthy of a saga and let them go about their business in peace.\u201d \u201cand which will let them\u201d or the like","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18839-zilaenor","name":"zilaenor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T18:36:32-07:00","id":1237354,"title":"","content":"The Morrigan, listed as a goddess of War, doesn't have Warrior as one of her Callings. P. 174","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24013-amaranth01","name":"Amaranth01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T14:11:26-07:00","id":1237581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amaranth01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1233836-scion-origin-errata-thread?p=1237354#post1237354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Morrigan, listed as a goddess of War, doesn't have Warrior as one of her Callings. P. 174</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to be a warrior to appear as an omen that wars are about to go off. A brilliant general may be a Sage or Leader with the War Purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T06:27:47-07:00","id":1237748,"title":"","content":"On the character record sheet under 'Attributes,' what I believe are the Favored Approaches are listed as 'Power,' 'Finesse,' and 'Resistance.' Pg. 97 lists the Favored Approaches as 'Force,' 'Finesse,' and 'Resilience.' Which are they?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo\">Maitrecorbo</a> mentioned this earlier but there are lots of references to 'Reason' which should probably be 'Intellect.' Here are the other ones I could find (pg number - section/sub-section):<br /> <br /> pg. 73 - Chases<br /> pg. 97 - Character Creation Example (R hand side)<br /> pg. 122 - First Aid<br /> pg. 141 - Riddle Me This<br /> Pg. 152 - Red Herring","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24419,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24419-cloud0685","user":"Cloud0685","date":". 07-22-2018, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24419-cloud0685","name":"Cloud0685","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T07:54:32-07:00","id":1237963,"title":"","content":"Rashmi Battacharya has &quot;Perfect Memory&quot; listed as a Knack. I imagine this is supposed to be the &quot;Palace of Memory&quot; Knack from the Sage Calling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8871-griffalo","name":"griffalo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8871_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T18:07:54-07:00","id":1238101,"title":"","content":"Some of the pregenerated characters still need work. Rashmi's skills and attributes are off (should have one more attribute dot and a couple more skill dots) so it might be worth taking a look at the process of making them. Seems like there may have been some mistakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T00:08:54-07:00","id":1238811,"title":"","content":"Page 15, Carniv\u00e1le: &quot;wise to the nature of The world they inhabit&quot;.<br /> Page 86, second column near the end of the second paragraph: &quot;The only one question remains&quot;.<br /> Pages 85/87/89/91/93, all Pre-Mades have too few Skill points allocated (should be 23: 18 for Path Skills plus 5 extra from Finishing Touches)<br /> Page 87, Emanuel has only five Attribute points allocated in his top-ranked arena.<br /> Page 89, Hassans Healer Calling and Loki as his Divine Parent don't mesh with the rules.<br /> Page 97, the rules state that you get six dots for the Attributes in your top-ranked arena, but in the Example, only five points are allocated.<br /> Page 98, second column, second Box with Character Creation Sample: The allocation of extra Skill dots and additional Knacks (or Birthrights) is missing.<br /> Page 120, Range Table: Medium only lists Cunning as an Attribute (the text on the previous page mentions Dexterity or Cunning for Medium), and Long lists Discipline (should be Cunning according to previus page).<br /> Page 125, Sample Armors: The Motorcycle Jacket lists Armored as a tag.<br /> Page 156: Centaurs get a Design Philosophy when everyone else gets Design Principles.<br /> Page 170, Freya's Calling List includes three Purviews (Death, Prosperity, Fertility).<br /> Page 171, Nana'b'oozoo is missing his third Calling and Ioskeha has an unneeded comma after his third Calling.<br /> Page 172, Persephone's Purviews are bolded.<br /> Page 173, Sarutahiko has four Callings.<br /> Page 174, the formatting of Osh\u00f3ss\u00ed's Entry is off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24456-xizzillix","user":"Xizzillix","date":". 07-26-2018, 05:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24456-xizzillix","name":"Xizzillix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T19:05:01-07:00","id":1239527,"title":"","content":"I don't know if any of these have been mentioned but:<br /> <br /> Hulderfolk reference a creator knack called &quot;structural integrity&quot;, this knack does not appear to exist.<br /> Deer woman have the trample knack, in older write ups this added the &quot;brutal tag&quot; which didn't exist. In this version there is a brutal tag but the knack now adds shockwave.<br /> Clarification, do specialties give+1 enhancement to applicable skill rolls or related rolls in separate skills? Character creation says one thing and the rules section another.<br /> Armor examples still have that ambiguous &quot;armored&quot; tag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T06:01:11-07:00","id":1239646,"title":"","content":"In appendix 2 Freya and Sarutahiko have too many callings, and Nana'b'oozoo has too few listed. Also, Oduduwa has a layout error, the callings line does not have the background as every other god does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24405-alrixus","name":"Alrixus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T06:32:03-07:00","id":1240010,"title":"","content":"None of the ready made characters have enough skill dots. They get 18 from paths, broken down to 9 primary, 6 secondary and 3 tertiary, and an extra five in finishing touches. That is a total of 23. Most of them have 21, apart from Hassan, who has 17, Rhiannon has 16. Rashmi is the only one with the full skill dots used.<br /> Each Scion should have 28 attribute dots total. 9 baseline, plus 6 primary arena, 4 secondary arena and 2 tertiary arena. That makes 21, plus the six for favored approach makes 27. And an extra point from the finishing touches step makes 28. Emanuel has 26, so is missing two dots. The others are all on 27, so are only missing 1 dot.<br /> Eric has a movement score too low. Twice athletics is 10, plus highest physical attribute is 15. Hassan should have 5, highest physical is dexterity. Rashmi should be 6, two times athletics, plus highest physical is 2+4=6. Rhiannon should have movement 11, two times athletics is 6, and highest physical is 5.<br /> The finishing touches says they get either two knacks or 4 points of birthrights. Birthrights are in hero only, so move that mention to the template used to upgrade from origin to hero level?<br /> The health track has an extra injured box, despite only getting one from the automatic stamina point. This takes up room for the extra bruised track from stamina. Just looked in depth at the character sheets and picked up on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24405-alrixus","name":"Alrixus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T06:49:50-07:00","id":1240017,"title":"","content":"Looking through knacks, and rules on healing. As the only rule on healing is in chapter four, and talks about first aid, it mentions an injury condition can only be downgraded once. And first aid only occurs after combat. How does this interact with Combat Medic healer knack, tending wounds in combat, and a repetitive once per turn removal of condition, when it is stated in first aid that only one injury condition can be removed by first aid per session. And does the damage conversion knack affect the difficulty for a first aid action, if it affects all injury conditions.<br /> Also, if a character has medicine 5, does that allow surgery later to help heal injury conditions after combat.<br /> Also, think this has been mentioned, but the first aid section references a medicine + reason roll, and reason seems to been replaced by intellect.<br /> Other than the immunization booster knack, can a character with medicine skill help with poison without magic like they can with disease?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24405-alrixus","name":"Alrixus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T07:08:58-07:00","id":1240024,"title":"","content":"Wireless Interface Creator Knack Pg 106 says &quot;Electronic devices respond you without needing to touch them.&quot; This either needs to swap the words you and without, like this &quot;Electronic devices respond without you needing to touch them.&quot; Or say it like this &quot;Electronic devices respond to you without you touching them.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24405-alrixus","name":"Alrixus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T07:15:06-07:00","id":1240029,"title":"","content":"Not a fighter lover knack Pg 110 mentions Followers, which as a birthright aren't mentioned till hero. Either remove on refer to hero book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24405-alrixus","name":"Alrixus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T07:20:36-07:00","id":1240034,"title":"","content":"Pg 122 talks about scale and damage. Basically repeats a paragraph, the wording is either identical or contradictory. The paragraphs above and below the &quot;Damage and Scale&quot; heading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24405-alrixus","name":"Alrixus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T07:35:50-07:00","id":1240039,"title":"","content":"Appendix 1, Pg 162 says Supernatural Origin Paths are equal to callings, including knacks. However Pg 98 says you choose a calling appropriate to the Supernatural Origin Path. Does this mean you add in the Path knacks to the calling, or could a Scion of Inari take kitsune in place of a calling, or Pan's scions take Satyr in place of a calling? Also, in the Appendix it mentions an Oracle origin path, which isn't included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24405-alrixus","name":"Alrixus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T07:47:18-07:00","id":1240044,"title":"","content":"Appendix 1, Pg 167 states it gives a total of 7 adjusted supernatural origin paths, 3 wolf warriors, 3 satyr and on animal character. In fact there are only 5, 3 wolf warrior and 2 satyr.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24405-alrixus","name":"Alrixus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T08:46:59-07:00","id":1240064,"title":"","content":"<b>Page 46: </b>&quot;Sages and Scions refer to the current age as the Titan Wars or the Cold War \u2014 something like the Second Titanomachy is simply more resonant than an event named after the 20th-century mortal affair, associated with nations that the Gods will outlast.&quot;<br /> <br /> This sentence doesn't entirely make sense. If &quot;Second Titanomachy&quot; is more resonant, why isn't it the term sages and Scions use?<br /> <br /> <b>Page 46: &quot;</b>They partake of The World\u2019s essence after all,&quot; needs a comma.<br /> <br /> <b>Page 46: </b>&quot;While some Titans present hate-filled, genocidal personalities, their nature means that humans just don\u2019t matter \u2014 or at least, they shouldn\u2019t.&quot;<br /> <br /> This should probably be &quot;While <i>not all</i> Titans...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T21:52:27-07:00","id":1240326,"title":"","content":"<b>Page 52:</b> The regular text between the &quot;DIVINE OPS&quot; and &quot;FAITH AND THE WORLD, PART 2&quot; sidebars just cuts off at &quot;the way irritation in an oyster <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">--</span>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T19:57:32-07:00","id":1240696,"title":"","content":"<b>p 34, 2nd complete paragraph</b>: &quot;A Primordial\u2019s inhabitants are include Elementals,..&quot; <br /> &quot;..are include...&quot; - should probably only be one of those. Eiither, &quot;A Primordial\u2019s<br /> inhabitants are Elementals,...&quot; or &quot;A Primordial\u2019s inhabitants include Elementals,..&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23804-uri-meca","name":"Uri Meca","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T20:08:49-07:00","id":1240701,"title":"","content":"<b>p33, entry on Doggerland, bottom of the first column into the top of the second:<br /> &quot;</b>Their true names were lost, <u>corrupted</u> by Christian <u>corruptions</u> of their legends.&quot;<br /> corrupted by.. corruptions.<br /> This repetition of 'corrupt-' threatens the quality of the writing, in my opinion. Recommend:<br /> &quot;...corrupted by Christian appropriation of their legends.&quot;<br /> or<br /> &quot;...corrupted by Christian re-imagining...&quot;<br /> or<br /> &quot;...corrupted by Christian reinterpretation...&quot;<br /> or anything but a repetition of &quot;corrupt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23804-uri-meca","name":"Uri Meca","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T03:46:51-07:00","id":1240786,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if this is truly an errata or if I misunderstood something.<br /> <br /> On page 97 under &quot;Step three: Skills&quot;<br /> &quot;<i>Your character receives three dots in each Skill associated with<br /> their primary Path, two dots in each Skill associated with<br /> their secondary path, and one dot in each Skill associated<br /> with their tertiary path. These dots are cumulative for<br /> Skills associated with two Paths. <b>If this gives a Skill more<br /> than five dots, redistribute the extra dot to another Path<br /> Skill</b></i>.&quot; (Bolding is mine)<br /> <br /> If a character recives 3 dots for primary skills, 2 for secondary and one for tertiary, and a single skill cannot be associated with more than two paths, then the bolded text describes an inpossible situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24436-boquerini","user":"Boquerini","date":". 07-31-2018, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24436-boquerini","name":"Boquerini","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T05:19:03-07:00","id":1240809,"title":"","content":"pg44, second paragraph states that Salvador is the birthplace of Capoeira. It isn't. It was supposedly created in the Quilombo de Palmares, which is in the current state of Pernambuco.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24400-endou_kenji","name":"endou_kenji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T11:13:12-07:00","id":1240962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boquerini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1233836-scion-origin-errata-thread?p=1240786#post1240786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if this is truly an errata or if I misunderstood something.<br /> <br /> On page 97 under &amp;quot;Step three: Skills&amp;quot;<br /> &amp;quot;<i>Your character receives three dots in each Skill associated with<br /> their primary Path, two dots in each Skill associated with<br /> their secondary path, and one dot in each Skill associated<br /> with their tertiary path. These dots are cumulative for<br /> Skills associated with two Paths. <b>If this gives a Skill more<br /> than five dots, redistribute the extra dot to another Path<br /> Skill</b></i>.&amp;quot; (Bolding is mine)<br /> <br /> If a character recives 3 dots for primary skills, 2 for secondary and one for tertiary, and a single skill cannot be associated with more than two paths, then the bolded text describes an inpossible situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Skills can be associated with multiple paths","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T11:26:11-07:00","id":1240970,"title":"","content":"The rules for rising from prone while an opponent is within close range are given twice, once with the movement rules and once with the combat rules, and they are inconsistent:<br /> <br /> On pg. 72:<br /> <i>&quot;However,<br /> if an opponent is engaging you in close range, they may make<br /> this difficult. If the opponent chooses to threaten your rise,<br /> any attacks you make on the same action after getting up are<br /> considered mixed actions, using the lower of your Athletics+<br /> Dexterity or Might and your relevant combat pool.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> On pg. 118:<br /> <i>&quot;However, if you are prone with an enemy<br /> in clash range then standing up gets more difficult. If there<br /> is an opponent in clash range with a prone character, then<br /> the prone character must stand up as part of a mixed action.<br /> Standing up is an Athletics roll with a Complication of 1.<br /> If the player fails to buy off the Complication, his character<br /> takes an Injury Condition as his opponents punishes his<br /> attempt to stand.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The rules on 118 also contain two other apparent typos: &quot;clash range&quot; rather than &quot;close range&quot; and &quot;his opponents punishes&quot; instead of &quot;his opponent punishes&quot; or &quot;his opponents punish.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T12:38:31-07:00","id":1240992,"title":"","content":"There are conflicting rules for Ambush (pp. 118) and &quot;Surprise Attacks&quot; (pp.120)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T17:04:39-07:00","id":1241077,"title":"","content":"On RichT's recommendation, I'm posting this here:<br /> <br /> It concerns me that the movement rules which are relevant in combat, including entirely combat-specific actions like Disengage, Rush, and Utilize Cover, are only given in Chapter 2, starting on page 72, while the rules for every other aspect of combat are in Chapter 4, starting on page 115. Furthermore, the movement actions reference range bands, which are only explained in the combat section, pgs. 119-120. This placement is inconvenient even in the PDF format, with bookmarking, and I can only imagine it would be even more frustrating when using a physical text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T01:18:27-07:00","id":1242262,"title":"","content":"I'm sure others have already caught many of these, but here's my list<br /> <br /> Page 3: One of the messages in the image says &quot;Shear physical perfection&quot; instead of &quot;Sheer physical perfection&quot;. It's unlikely he's talking about scissors. It's also totally reasonable that Donnie would use the wrong word. There's also &quot;Donnie's got stlye&quot; and &quot;have yo baby&quot;, which again may be deliberate.<br /> Page 9: Aos Si doesn't seem to have an acute on the 'i'<br /> Page 9: Cu Sith doesn't have the grave on the 'u' or 'i', but the Cu Sidhe form (Irish) looks like it would have an acute on the 'u' (I don't have a decent source to be sure on the Irish version). Some sources leave out the graves entirely when used in English. If modified here, the entry on page 167 should be updated as well.<br /> Page 9: Issue with &quot;The Yoruba Pantheon&quot; (missing unicode character?)<br /> Page 9: Deva should have an acute, rather than a grave<br /> Page 9: Shen should either have an acute here, or it should be excluded in the rest of the book.<br /> Page 11: &quot;very different place than the anything&quot; should probably be &quot;very different place than anything&quot;<br /> Page 12: Possible error in &quot;blessings upon mankind... while&quot; where perhaps the ellipsis was supposed to be a comma. While ellipsis is occasionally used to indicate a long pause, it should be preceded by a space in that case.<br /> Page 15: Under Carnivale, &quot;The world&quot; should be &quot;The World&quot; or &quot;the world&quot; depending on which one you're talking about<br /> Page 16: Terra Incognitae isn't the proper plural form of Terra Incognita, since you would make the noun plural as well as the adjective (Terrae Incognitae). However, Terra Incognitae does look better for a non-Latin reader, and if you're making it your own term, I suppose you can decide on your own plural form.<br /> Page 22: I didn't find an authoritative source that matched the spelling used for Lugh Lamhfhada's epithet (Lamhfhada). However, various sources spell it differently, and if your spelling was intentional, it's probably fine and will be familiar to players of various video games.<br /> Page 27: &quot;just desserts&quot; should be &quot;just deserts&quot; (from deserve)<br /> Page 34: &quot;A Primordial's inhabitants are include Elementals&quot; should exclude either the &quot;are&quot; or the &quot;include&quot;<br /> Page 36: Under Overworld Gates, &quot;and the exceptions are either pass through&quot; should exclude the &quot;are&quot; (or perhaps pass should be another word?)<br /> Page 37: I'm assuming the &quot;ao si&quot; is supposed to be &quot;aos si&quot;. If so, since &quot;aes sidhe&quot; was the term used earlier in the book, perhaps the same term should be used in both places. The earlier reference could be changed instead. The term &quot;aos si&quot; seems more correct, while the older &quot;aes sidhe&quot; is likely more familiar. Aos Si is also the Antagonist entry.<br /> Page 40: Should yokai and Jizo have a macron over the 'o'?<br /> Page 41: If dodaem is intended to be the same thing as doodem, it's an infrequent spelling. Similarly, Anishinaabeg seems more common than Anishinaubaek.<br /> Page 42: The 'o' with a macron in Teotl didn't show up here for me in one reader, and showed up oddly in another. This could just be an issue with the readers I'm using.<br /> Page 42: Should ollamaliztli have a macron over the 'o'?<br /> Page 42: Possibly, tzitzimime should be tzitzimimeh instead<br /> Page 43: I believe Jaen should have an acute on the 'e'<br /> Page 44: I believe the tilde belongs over the 'a' in Sao, rather than the first 'a' in Salvador.<br /> Page 45: Under Varanasi, the term Kami is not capitalized, as it is in the rest of the book.<br /> Page 48: &quot;This may be one the reasons Titans&quot; should be &quot;This may be one of the reasons Titans&quot;<br /> Page 51: Text ends abrubtly after &quot;irritation in an oyster&quot;<br /> Page 57: In the Rolling Dice sidebar, &quot;The Storyguide might determine the Approach while the player decides the Approach&quot;. I'm assuming the first of these was supposed to be &quot;Arena&quot; (from text on pages 61 and 62), though the Forming a Dice Pool section seems to indicate the player just gets to choose the Attribute.<br /> Page 60: Under Medicine, there's a switch from &quot;Their&quot; to &quot;she&quot;. Under Pilot, while the &quot;They&quot; pronoun isn't used, the &quot;he&quot; and &quot;his&quot; don't match the style of the other entries.<br /> Page 61: Under Survival 1, Survival 5, and Technology 5, the feminine pronoun is used. I don't have any objection to any particular choice of pronoun, but it looks like an effort was made to use &quot;they&quot; for this section (particularly for Techonology 5 where &quot;they&quot; is also used).<br /> Page 66: In the Scale Level table's Speed Example for level 6, I believe &quot;Dandu Morana&quot; should be either &quot;Dandu Monara&quot; or &quot;Dhadu Monara&quot; (r and n swapped)<br /> Page 67: Under Stunts, the &quot;complicated Stunt&quot; and &quot;difficult Stunt&quot; are in italics, while the &quot;enhanced Stunt&quot; is not.<br /> Page 71: Under Action-adventure, perhaps the plural version Terra Incognitae should be used here.<br /> Page 72: Under Barriers in the Movement section, the suggested dice pool is &quot;Athletics + Might or Finesse&quot;. Was this supposed to be &quot;Athletics + Might or Dexterity&quot;?<br /> Page 75: In the Investigation Example, the Greek version of &quot;Amethysta&quot; should be &quot;Amethystos&quot; (the Roman version is &quot;Amethyste&quot;)<br /> Page 77: Under Intrigue &quot;character's Attitudes&quot; should probably be &quot;characters' Attitudes&quot;<br /> Page 79: Under Exerting Influence in the Encourage Belief paragraph, there should probably be an &quot;or&quot; between &quot;Leadership (indoctrination)&quot; and &quot;Subterfuge (rumors)&quot;.<br /> <br /> There are some errors with the skill specializations which others have already mentioned.<br /> Page 85: Eric Donner has spent 21 skill points. If Step Six of character creation is unintended, this should be 18. If Step Six is intended, this should be 23. He also has not allocated the extra attribute point.<br /> Page 86: Near the end of the Background section, &quot;The only one question remains&quot; seems to have one too many words. Removing any one of &quot;the&quot;, &quot;only&quot;, or &quot;one&quot; makes the sentence work better. There's also a missing period at the end of the last sentence in the &quot;Where's Xiutechutli&quot; sidebar.<br /> Page 87: Emanuel Montero has spent 21 skill points. He has spent one fewer attribute points than Eric Donner (perhaps he should have another point in Composure). The extra attribute point from Step Six is not included either.<br /> Page 89: Hassan al-Hakim has spent only 17 skill points. It's likely some were supposed to go into Empathy. The extra attribute point from Step Six is not included. I expected his Movement Dice to be 5, since the section on Movement seems to let you use the better of Dexterity and Might.<br /> Page 91: Rashmi Bhattacharya is missing the 'h' in her last name. She has spent only 21 skill points. The extra attribute point from Step Six is not included. I expected her Movement Dice to be 5 (using Dexterity).<br /> Page 93: Rhiannon Jernigan has spent only 18 skill points. The extra attribute point from Step Six is not included.<br /> Page 94: In the section on deeds, &quot;in-setting destines&quot; should probably be &quot;in-setting destinies&quot;<br /> Page 94: &quot;Since Deeds are an expression of intent towards and action&quot; might have been intended as &quot;towards an action&quot;<br /> Page 97: The Character Creation Example under Attributes uses Reason rather than Intellect. For some reason, only 5 points are assigned the the Social Arena (3 Presence, 1 Manipulation, 1 Composure), so the final stats are off by one.<br /> Page 98: The Character Creation Example under Finishing touches indicates that Mao has three Injury conditions. I'm not sure if this is one lower than it should be, or if Taken Out is just not counted. There's also mention of the Athletics + Stamina pool, which is apparently 4. This would make sense if Mao had an Athletics of 2, but he doesn't appear to have this skill (though he did have 5 discretionary points, which may have been allocated to Athletics). Given the character sheet, I would expect the pool he's computing to be the Move pool, which the other characters base on Athletics + Might. Finally, it looks like he's using Composure for his Defense stat, which may be intended, but all of the other sample characters restricted themselves to Stamina for this.<br /> Page 104: The Sneak role and Technology Expert role list Enigmas as a skill (perhaps this is supposed to be Occult)<br /> Page 104: Under Supernatural Origin Paths, &quot;Humans dominate The World, but they not the only&quot; should be &quot;but they are not the only&quot;<br /> Page 106: Under Wireless Interface, &quot;Electronic devices respond you without needing to touch them&quot; should be &quot;respond to you without needing to touch them&quot; or simply &quot;respond without needing to touch them&quot;<br /> Page 106: Under Guardian &quot;Mortal Guardian Knacks gift you with the vast fortitude and sharp senses, to better protect&quot; should either exclude the comma, or be &quot;gift you with vast fortitude and sharp senses, to better protect&quot; (excluding &quot;the&quot;)<br /> Page 107: Under Hunter, there is an instance of kami that is not capitalized<br /> Page 111: Under the Trickster Knack, &quot;In Sheep's Clothing&quot;, &quot;When you disguise yourself, you do without needing to roll&quot; should be &quot;you do so without needing to roll&quot;<br /> Page 112: Well Tempered references the &quot;Armored&quot; Tag. Should this be Soft (1)?<br /> Page 112: Under Character Advancement, &quot;The Storyguide have more control&quot; should be &quot;has more control&quot;<br /> Page 116: Under Attack Resolution, item 5, &quot;The next player's takes their turn&quot; should be &quot;The next player's character takes their turn&quot; or perhaps &quot;The next player takes their turn&quot;. Since the next slot may be an SGC slot, perhaps it would be best as &quot;The next character takes their turn&quot;.<br /> Page 117: The Grapple section lists a Skill of &quot;Agility (Might)&quot;. Was this supposed to be Athletics or Close Combat? The Grapple sidebar seems to have a different mechanism of escaping the grapple than the Break Free stunt. I'm also confused by the 1s cost of Break Free, given that the cost seems to either be 0s or the number your opponent spent. The Position stunt mentions Dodge, but that's not defined (we already need to overcome defense for all of these stunts).<br /> Page 118: Under Ranged Attack, the Disarm stunt mentions the &quot;near&quot; range increment, which should probably be &quot;Short&quot;<br /> Page 118: Under Modifiers to Attack / Defense Actions, there are three mentions of &quot;clash range&quot;, which should probably be &quot;Close range&quot;<br /> Page 118: Under Ambush, &quot;roll Agility + Dexterity&quot; should perhaps be &quot;roll Dexterity + Subterfuge&quot;<br /> Page 120: In the table entry for Long range, perhaps Discipline was meant to be Resolve. Overall, the textual portion doesn't match the table.<br /> Page 125: Motorcycle Jacket referenced Armored. Should this be Soft (1)?<br /> Page 146: The Armor box states that Soft Armor increases Defense. For players, it instead increases the successes needed for the Inflict Damage stunt. Increasing Defense makes stunts like Disarm more difficult, which may not be intended.<br /> Page 170: Freya's Callings entry includes several Purviews<br /> Page 171: Persephone purviews are bold<br /> Page 171: Artemis callings doesn't have the background, and Purviews does<br /> Page 173: Footer should probably be Netjer|Kami|Tuatha de Denann, since those are the sections started on these two pages<br /> Page 174: Orisha should have graves instead of acutes<br /> Page 174: Yoruba may not need any diacritical marks, but if you do use them, I believe the 'o' should not have a mark, while the 'u' has a grave and the 'a' has an acute.<br /> Page 174: Oduduwa didn't get the background for the Callings line.<br /> Page 174: Oshossi didn't get the right formatting: Callings and Purviews should be in bold; Callings should have a background; Oshossi should have a background<br /> Page 178: &quot;Wits and Perception and folded&quot; should be &quot;Wits and Perception are folded&quot;<br /> <br /> It would be nice if the Purviews were always in alphabetical order.<br /> I did not check any of the God names for proper diacritics.<br /> <br /> Other notes and questions:<br /> Page 58: A bulked-up power lifter (Physical 3) with the Force Favored Approach (Might 5) who is an Olympic athlete (Athletics 5) will average 3.33 successes, and succeeds at lifting two microwaves about 2/3rd of the time. This should be typically achievable by a Might 1, Athletics 0 mortal.<br /> Page 65: In the scale section, the mention of &quot;astra weapon&quot; is the only one in this book (those with access to Hero may understand it's a relic).<br /> Page 67: In the Stunts section, there's a prohibition on benefiting the same Skill/Attribute combination. It's possible the intent is that after your Stunt using Dexterity + Athletics, you can benefit your teammate's Dexterity + Athletics, but if so, that's unclear.<br /> Page 72: Under Utilize Cover in the Movement section, it isn't clear if the &quot;simple roll&quot; indicates that this is a simple action.<br /> Page 73: Under Procedurals, one of the examples is &quot;engage in intrigue&quot;. Normally, this would be a decent example, but since Intrigue is one of the three areas of action, it's odd to use it here.<br /> Page 74: Given that the Greco-Roman pantheon (Theoi) uses Hades rather than Pluto (Kerberos is generally associated with Hades), perhaps this should be changed to &quot;child of Hades&quot; instead of &quot;child of Pluto&quot;.<br /> Page 74: Under Finding Clues &quot;There is a variety of ways&quot; is more typically written &quot;There are a variety of ways&quot;. The version you have isn't wrong per se, but goes against the AMA Manual of Style.<br /> Page 83: Under Ready-made Characters &quot;Each character has used some experience to buy two additional Knacks&quot;. Given Step Six of character creation, this does not seem to require any additional experience.<br /> Page 85 et al.: This character sheet has two Bruised slots and two Injured slots. Given the effect of Stamina on Health described on page 98, I would expect three Bruised slots and only one Injured slot (with one or two of the Bruised slots being unavailable to most characters)<br /> Page 97: Under Skills, &quot;If this gives a Skill more than five dots, redistribute the extra dot to another Path Skill.&quot; isn't applicable, given the rule on page 96 that &quot;Any given Skill can be associated with at most two of your Paths.&quot;<br /> Page 97: Under Skills, the explanation of Momentum granted by a failed roll with a Specialty implies that the failed Ability roll does not need to match the Specialty (e.g. the character with a Specialty in Pistols misses with a Rifle, and since she's failed a roll with an Ability in which she has a Specialty, she gets 2 Momentum). It's also unclear what the Ability keyword is here, though I suspect it was meant to be Skill.<br /> Page 107: In the Healer Knack &quot;With A Glance&quot;, there is a shift from &quot;you&quot; to &quot;she&quot;. Similarly on page 109 in the Leader Knack &quot;Captain of Industry&quot;, &quot;You can inspire a number of people equal to her Leadership&quot; has the same shift.<br /> Page 112: Under Character Advancement, &quot;spending momentum&quot; should be &quot;spending Momentum&quot;<br /> Page 115: Under Attack Resolution, item 3 &quot;Spend successes to overcome the target's Defense, the attack is successful.&quot; is confusing. Perhaps this was meant to bridge into the next sentence: &quot;If the attack is successful, spend additional successes on Stunts.&quot;<br /> Page 116: The Inflict Damage stunt for Close Combat includes the Armor, but the Grapple, Ranged Attack, and Thrown Attack do not include this. It's not really necessary to mention it, since it is mentioned in the Armor section, but including it for one type and not the others implies that Armor only applies to Close Combat.<br /> Page 118: The Ranged Attack Pin stunt seems like it would always be added to any successful attack at a cost of 0s. It's also odd that the Thrown Attack knockdown (Line Drive) goes against Might while the Ranged Attack knockdown (Knock Down) goes against Stamina.<br /> Page 124: Under Armor Tags, if all of the tags count as Armored, it seems like you could save a point by skipping Soft (1), assuming that's the same thing<br /> Page 149: Attack - Can the Antagonist act while maintaining Dread Gaze? Mixed actions and Move without using a basic action are disallowed, but what about other actions, like attacking?<br /> Page 180 (back cover): This references &quot;the World&quot; rather than &quot;The World&quot; as in the rest of the book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24408-ubik2","user":"ubik2","date":". 08-03-2018, 04:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24408-ubik2","name":"ubik2","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T02:57:03-07:00","id":1243158,"title":"","content":"Not 100% if this is an oversight worth errata or an intentional decision already made, but should Nuwa the Snake Goddess have Beasts (snake) as a purview?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T23:33:48-07:00","id":1244058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ubik2</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1233836-scion-origin-errata-thread?p=1242262#post1242262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure others have already caught many of these, but here's my list......SNIP!!!!!!!!!</div> </div> </div> </div>Good Lord Man!!! And well done. On my first pass through I missed about 60% of these.<br /> <br /> Having said that, not sure if it has been mentioned before but on p.g. 150 there's a mention of awareness and cunning for a roll. I looked and unless there's a passive awareness trait or something like 5e...which I also have not seen, I don't think awareness is an actual skill","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":488,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/488-blackwood","user":"Blackwood","date":". 08-09-2018, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/488-blackwood","name":"Blackwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T01:00:20-07:00","id":1244074,"title":"","content":"I am relatively convinced someone must have found this by now but I didn't see it here: <br /> P. 57 &quot;Forming a Dice Pool&quot; Refers to Finesse as Control on two occasions.<br /> &quot;displays their Force, Control, or Resilience in that area&quot;<br /> &quot;it may also be a test of mental control&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, throws from a grapple are extremely contradictory and confusing. This covers the grapple sidebar on p.117, the throw stunt on the same page and the Throwing paragraph on p.118.<br /> The sidebar says, you can throw a grappled target with opposed Athletics + Might, winning ties. The paragraph on 118 mentions lifting with Athletics + Might, which isn't opposed, as weight is static. <br /> More importantly though, the sidebar allows a grappler to just throw their victim (as a simple action, I assume) whereas the Stunt has you pay successes from the Grapple action. As I understand it, Grapple replaces Close Combat Attacks against an already grappled target (as opposed to starting a grapple, which is done with CCA). It works with Agility + Might, which probably means Athletics + Might, as Agility doesn't exist. It's also the only attack action to list the relevant Attribute in parentheses behind the skill. This has you overcome the target's defense to perform Grapple Stunts, including Throw. This version needs at least one success to throw [Might] meters + 1 meter per extra success, which is the only indication of the range of this throw from a grapple, so let's use it. <br /> 1. Why would you need to succeed on the Grapple action and spend successes on a stunt to throw your victim if just being in control let's you throw them right away?<br /> 2. Why do you not need to be able to lift your opponent for this stunt?<br /> 3. How do you determine the distance on the sidebar throw, when there are no successes from a Grapple action to pay for it?<br /> 4. Why does the grappler win ties on the opposed roll from the sidebar, when normally, defenders win?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13477-vezalchemyst","user":"VeZAlchemyst","date":". 08-09-2018, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13477-vezalchemyst","name":"VeZAlchemyst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T15:53:03-07:00","id":1244304,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this is an errata for Origin or Hero, but Origin references &quot;Calling Crisis&quot; on page 153 as a possible source of Tension Pool, indicating it's defined in Hero. This term doesn't appear in either book again - and should probably be in Origin, if it's a rule that is intended for use in Origin games.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Looking at it closer, this probably refers to changing Callings through Failure and Adoption Deeds, but neither seems to give Tension as currently defined in the Hero Draft. Likewise, the other source of Tension on 153 of the Origin book references resolving Conditions as a source of Tension, but resolving conditions only appears to give momentum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","user":"HighPriest","date":". 08-09-2018, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T18:40:52-07:00","id":1244341,"title":"","content":"Hm, another note on character creation. The paragraph at the top of <b>pg. 98</b> is messy, but I'm not sure which way it should be corrected. It presently reads...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Choose one Calling from the list below or Supernatural<br /> Origin Path. If your character is a pre-Visitation Scion, this<br /> Calling must come from their divine patron\u2019s three Favored<br /> Callings. It also determines the source of your Knack. Choose<br /> from a Calling list that seems appropriate (e.g. Trickster for a<br /> Kitsune, Hunter, or Warrior for an Amazon, etc.) and assign<br /> it one dot. </div> </div> </div>The sentence which begins with &quot;Choose from a Calling list that seems appropriate&quot; obviously refers to creating a Denizen / creature of Legend character due to its parenthetical examples, but it isn't introduced smoothly. In fact, I must say that I'm confused as to whether the Denizen creation rules are intended to be in Chapter 3 at all, or if they were all supposed to be moved to the Supernatural Paths Appendix. &quot;Creatures of Legend&quot; are mentioned on pg. 94 in the Concept step, and they're clumsily mentioned there in the Callings and Knacks section on pg. 98, and pg. 104 gives a brief introduction for Supernatural Origin Paths and then refers you to the Appendix for everything other than pre-Visitation Scion, but I believe those are the only references. It's possible that the bits on 94 and 98 are textual artifacts, and 104 is meant to be the arrow pointing toward Denizen rules for those Storyguides and players who want them, or maybe they're meant to be more clearly present as an option throughout the whole chapter. I'm not sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21733,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","user":"Ascension","date":". 08-10-2018, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T13:46:36-07:00","id":1244610,"title":"","content":"Been going through the Supernatural Paths, here's what I've found:<ul><li>It is not clear if the Adjusted Paths still give access to the base Path's knacks.</li> <li>The 'Armorbound' (Warrior knack) in the Classical Amazon write up does not exist (pg 167)</li> <li>The 'Their Fort Standing (Guardian Knack)' in the Shieldmaidan write up does not exist (pg 168)</li> </ul><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/963-kylar","name":"Kylar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar963_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T14:07:11-07:00","id":1244614,"title":"","content":"And another one: The Break Up Grapple stunt and the Grappled condition (pg 116-117) disagree on how to get out of being grappled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/963-kylar","name":"Kylar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar963_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T10:30:34-07:00","id":1246377,"title":"","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> I've been combing through things and while I still have other items to double check before I post them I did want to slot in what I could.<br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Page 11 - The World of Legend exists alongside The world of humanity. -&gt; It should either be The World of Humanity, or the world of humanity. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Page 12 - &quot;ready to devour hapless mortals who stopped at the wrong spring to drink or took the wrong paths through the dark, deep woods.&quot; -&gt; Shouldn't this be deep, dark woods instead of dark, deep woods? </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Page 15 - &quot;Carniv\u00e0le\u2019s miracles are low and slow, never quite making the \u201crubes\u201d wise to the nature of The world they inhabit.&quot; -&gt; nature of The world is weirdly capitalized, should it be The World or the world, either way - needs consistency.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Page 16 - &quot;The Gods long ago retreated from the mortal World&quot; -&gt; World is capitalized but mortal is not, If referencing a formal reference then it should be Mortal World, or if not intended to be - should be mortal world.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Page 16 - &quot;Legendary creature: Any non-human being related to the mythic World,&quot; -&gt; should be either Mythic World or mythic world.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Page 16 - each instance of a term not capitalized.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Page 30 - &quot;They almost possess powerful&quot; - should be &quot;They almost <b>all</b> possess&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Page 34 - &quot;but even Primordials binding Fire and Darkness...&quot; - this is awkward with the use of Binding - should pick a different word to describe this that fits the sentence - such as &quot;But even Primordials of Fire and Darkness&quot; or &quot;But even Primordials who embody Fire and Darkness..&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Page 34 - &quot;A Primordial's inhabitants are include...&quot; - should be altered to say either &quot;A Primordial's inhabitants include&quot; or &quot;A Primordial's inhabitants can include..&quot;.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Page 36 - &quot; the exceptions <b>are </b>either pass through other realms attuned to&quot; - should be &quot;the exceptions either pass through...&quot; - remove are as the flow of the rest of the sentence is specific to describing what the exceptions DO, not what they actually are.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Page 49 - &quot;This isn\u2019t <b>a</b> just a war of ideals,&quot; - remove the first a, should read &quot;This isn't just a war of ideals...&quot;</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><br /> Page 57 - Under Rolling the Dice 2. &quot;The Storyguide might determine the Approach while the player decides the Approach&quot; One of the instances of &quot;Approach&quot; should be Arena. I assume based on the formatting of later wording it should say &quot;The Storyguide might determine the Arena while the player decides the Approach&quot;...</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Page 57 - &quot;displays their Force, Control, or Resilience&quot; - I believe &quot;Control&quot; should be &quot;Finesse&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Page 59 - The text for Leadership (Copied here) appears to be different in size or font than the rest of the same text throughout the skill pages. &quot;Leadership is a knowledge of...&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Page 61 - The text for Technology (Copied here) appears to be different in size or font than the rest of the same text throughout the skill pages &quot;Technology represents the...&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Page 66 - &quot;a master swordswoman might be able a cut everything within reach&quot; - This should be altered to read as either &quot;might be able to cut everything&quot; or &quot;may be able to cut everything within reach&quot;. the word &quot;a&quot; is either incorrect or the phrase should be modified to remove it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Page 69 - FAILURE - has a weird graphic distortion on the LUR where it is unclear if that is intentional or if it is accidental, the U appears to be angled and slightly above the other letters.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Page 70 - MOMENTUM - the TUM has a weird graphic on the U same as on page 69.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Page 70 - which can hold up to (twice the number of players) at a time. - This is formatted strangely as you do not need to add the parentheses but should clarify &quot;which can hold up to twice the number of players in Momentum at a time.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Page 72 - When it\u2019s relevant, an unimpeded human on foot can move a number of feet each turn equal to twice their Athletics + their highest Physical Attribute. - I would try to clarify this so it is exceedingly clear. Is the intent &quot;(2xAthletics) + Highest Physical Attribute, or is the intent 2x(Athletics+Physical Att)? I would spell this out in specificity for the sake of text rather than leave it potentially ambiguous.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Definitely let me know if there is any question regarding these notes. <br /> <br /> -Ender</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24514-enderastraeus","name":"EnderAstraeus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T23:17:34-07:00","id":1246546,"title":"","content":"The Ready Made Character Eric, on p. 85, has the Knack Tempered, which is probably supposed to be Well Tempered.<br /> <br /> Emanuel, on p. 87, has listed the knacks Bold Introduction and Inspirational Aura. I can't find either in Origin, though Inspirational Aura does appear in the Hero preview as a copy of Captain of Industry.<br /> <br /> Hassan, on p. 89, has &quot;Healer with the Hands of God&quot;, which is probably supposed to be &quot;Surgeon with the Hands of God&quot;. He also has Instant Diagnosis, which I can't find in Origin, but does appear in Hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T09:04:29-07:00","id":1247729,"title":"","content":"Page 123 - the weapon tag Brutal is not <b>bold</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}